    <pageTitle>
      <Value><![CDATA[Asphalt & Bitumen Marshall and Bulk Density Flow Tests]]></Value>
    </pageTitle>
    <serviceCategories>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  {
    "key": "aa0b110a-92d7-479e-8c5c-dc609e572c28",
    "name": "Item 1",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "01",
    "categoryHeading1": "Asphalt briquettes for Marshall test",
    "categoryHeading2": "for Marshall test",
    "category": "<p>Compaction of hot mix asphalt material into cylindrical briquettes which allows the material to undergo Marshall analysis tests.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/1d848a4b38e94ad0956821fe06d6ae9c"
  },
  {
    "key": "24914d40-ec78-44f7-88b4-382282f6d1ef",
    "name": "Item 2",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "02",
    "categoryHeading1": "Marshall stability, flow and quotient",
    "categoryHeading2": "flow and quotient",
    "category": "<p>Determining the stability and flow of compacted asphalt briquettes with an electronic plotter. Marshall stability is related to the resistance of bituminous materials to distortion, displacement, rutting and shearing stresses.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/fcb07635b13f4c638367e6c76e0c180a"
  },
  {
    "key": "f4de36e2-42e0-4198-abe8-8f48c455c459",
    "name": "Item 3",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "03",
    "categoryHeading1": "Bulk density and void content of compacted asphalt (BRD)",
    "categoryHeading2": "of compacted asphalt (BRD)",
    "category": "<p>Used to determine the density of the hot mix asphalt mix after compaction.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/c36e12615bba4dd283cad2184c4d0e6b"
  },
  {
    "key": "5fd76eb0-37e6-4062-b17a-7de4e9460a0f",
    "name": "Item 4",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "04",
    "categoryHeading1": "Theoretical Maximum Specific Gravity",
    "categoryHeading2": "Specific Gravity",
    "category": "<p>A hot mix asphalt sample is placed into a pycnometer and a vacuum pump removes all air from the sample to determine the mix density. This result, coupled with the result obtained from the BRD, is used to calculate the voids in the hot mix.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/8a7321a9886a43e283bebffc2720182b"
  },
  {
    "key": "9baac125-3041-4b0e-bab8-e7c1abc52462",
    "name": "Item 5",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "05",
    "categoryHeading1": "Soluble binder content and particle size analysis",
    "categoryHeading2": "and particle size analysis",
    "category": "<p>Used to determine the percentage of binder in the hot mix asphalt sample. Sample is “washed” with a suitable solvent and processed through a centrifuge to separate the dissolved liquid and binder mixture from the fine aggregates to ensure no aggregate material is lost to perform an accurate sieve analysis on the sample.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/dc6feae4fb9f429eaddead909f29ff41"
  },
  {
    "key": "bf8438d6-8b49-44ea-bfb7-9d3aa01fb31c",
    "name": "Item 6",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "06",
    "categoryHeading1": "Bitumen content of asphalt mix ",
    "categoryHeading2": "asphalt mix ",
    "category": "<p>Used to determine the percentage of binder in the hot mix asphalt sample by means of an ignition oven. A sample is placed into the oven and the bitumen is physically burned off. The weight of the sample after the burning process is then compared to the starting weight to determine the loss.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/cd1ef64d92604ed0bb589de252312282"
  },
  {
    "key": "7c65caba-33bf-4df6-b800-066aac1c304d",
    "name": "Item 7",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "07",
    "categoryHeading1": "Binder content of mixtures",
    "categoryHeading2": "of mixtures",
    "category": "<p>This method is used to accurately determine the net bitumen content of a slurry mixture.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/e5dff888245f4dd4a4999f5a07d9c0c6"
  },
  {
    "key": "9b013406-6346-4e3c-9024-275b46c8a86d",
    "name": "Item 8",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "08",
    "categoryHeading1": "Low- temperature and dynamic viscosity",
    "categoryHeading2": "and dynamic viscosity",
    "category": "<p>Viscosity is the measure of resistance of flow or shear of a fluid. This test is used to determine the shear-rate and apparent viscosity of bitumen.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/60eb71b13ee14305972ea50b525093d4"
  },
  {
    "key": "f9f9b29c-77b6-4581-88a8-e41d95f63427",
    "name": "Item 9",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "09",
    "categoryHeading1": "Rolling thin film oven ",
    "categoryHeading2": "thin film oven ",
    "category": "<p>This test method is intended to measure the effects of heat and air on a thin film of bitumen. It aims to simulate the hardening properties of bituminous binders during the mixing, transportation and compacting process.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/9e158bec22a14e82a373ae6624c6feea"
  },
  {
    "key": "e9df9bf2-dd4a-48fd-8520-9a02d87da4f0",
    "name": "Item 10",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "10",
    "categoryHeading1": "Elastic recovery ",
    "categoryHeading2": "recovery ",
    "category": "<p>This test method is used to determine the elastic properties of a polymer modified bituminous binder.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/fddee27a996c43c2a48688c83631ae23"
  },
  {
    "key": "b51a61dd-52c6-4346-aa2f-8c832e55be0f",
    "name": "Item 11",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "11",
    "categoryHeading1": "Ball penetration and resilience",
    "categoryHeading2": "and resilience",
    "category": "<p>This test measures the relative hardness or consistency of bitumen rubber blends.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/815bd70ee0ff46c1b2d47b2d55560e80"
  },
  {
    "key": "282283f6-dc5c-4317-90af-2de16132dad6",
    "name": "Item 12",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "12",
    "categoryHeading1": "Compression recovery ",
    "categoryHeading2": "recovery ",
    "category": "<p>This test is used to measure the contribution made by the rubber crumbs to the bitumen rubber blend’s ability to return to its original shape after compression.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/0ac43b46396a4cd28c95ec8b897c6bc6"
  },
  {
    "key": "65ac49c7-6d76-43ce-a02f-df6891ebc177",
    "name": "Item 13",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "13",
    "categoryHeading1": "Flow test",
    "categoryHeading2": "test",
    "category": "<p>This test is used to measure the flow properties of bitumen at high temperatures.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/97ba3183db2a4aad9436eedf67667930"
  },
  {
    "key": "0e477189-3297-4067-81c4-350fa21b79a1",
    "name": "Item 14",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "14",
    "categoryHeading1": "Ball penetration test ",
    "categoryHeading2": "test ",
    "category": "<p>The ball penetration test is used to simulate the embedment of stone chips that occurs during construction and under traffic loading.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/23c6843c6ef14d14aab43be4a4819dc3"
  },
  {
    "key": "ddcd8dcb-1e31-451f-a2ab-8a3bf9e90268",
    "name": "Item 15",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "15",
    "categoryHeading1": "Texture depth measurement",
    "categoryHeading2": "measurement",
    "category": "<p>This test is used to determine the texture of a road surface (the roughness).</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/fa6f73aad6d34a5a8b27d34328457126"
  },
  {
    "key": "a6036bdb-36f5-42ab-9e3d-368fe2f379ce",
    "name": "Item 16",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "16",
    "categoryHeading1": "Marvil test",
    "categoryHeading2": "test",
    "category": "<p>This test is used to determine the in-situ water permeability of bituminous surfacing. The permeability of that bituminous layer provides an indication of the interconnectivity of the voids in the layer. The results provide an indication of the material’s susceptibility to the ingress of water.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/bebb943d84f0446ba435d18c9f096301"
  },
  {
    "key": "f08a9226-8845-416e-9d0c-0339f719b2f7",
    "name": "Item 17",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "17",
    "categoryHeading1": "Certification of a binder distributor ",
    "categoryHeading2": "a binder distributor ",
    "category": "<p>These tests are conducted for the fit for purpose certification of a binder distributor (Sprayer tanker). Tests are conducted annually and include: certification of a binder distributor (BT 20), validation of binder distributor dipstick (BT 21), power and speed indicator test (BT 22), pump system performance (BT23) and transverse distribution (bucket test) (BT 24).</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/4c8ce10fb2b7409f9e3fca563faf4312"
  },
  {
    "key": "bab9aef8-fe9a-41b0-aaa4-33f4c52b067e",
    "name": "Item 18",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "18",
    "categoryHeading1": "Penetration of bituminous materials",
    "categoryHeading2": "bituminous materials",
    "category": "<p>The needle penetration test is used as a measure of consistency, higher values of penetration indicate softer consistency.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/2ed3ef72a9e64304a4a04682f5ecee5e"
  },
  {
    "key": "fbd73fdc-b338-4e59-b5d7-5a2a8c4d5d23",
    "name": "Item 19",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "19",
    "categoryHeading1": "Softening point of bitumen",
    "categoryHeading2": "of bitumen",
    "category": "<p>Bitumen is a viscoelastic material without sharply defined melting points. The softening point is useful in the classification of bitumen as one element in establishing the uniformity of receiving shipments of binder.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/5e81ed95fb70424594f70876bd35a0c2"
  },
  {
    "key": "c9b3571e-2b1f-414c-9f1f-bbd85d1e8319",
    "name": "Item 20",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "20",
    "categoryHeading1": "Water content ",
    "categoryHeading2": "content ",
    "category": "<p>This test method measures the amount of water present in the emulsified asphalt as distinguished from either bitumen or petroleum solvent.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/88501e4fb491442aab67c3359a0c4835"
  },
  {
    "key": "04dbefa0-506e-4662-8975-3caff612e92f",
    "name": "Item 21",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "21",
    "categoryHeading1": "Hamburg abrasion testing ",
    "categoryHeading2": "testing ",
    "category": "<p>Specimens prepared in the laboratory or cores from field samples can be tested under simulated conditions in the laboratory to determine their susceptibility to rutting and moisture against different load, temperature and moisture settings.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/29dbae5eb11b46d1beabfd1aa979e76d"
  },
  {
    "key": "7e816d51-b342-43eb-8bed-38c048ff6925",
    "name": "Item 22",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "22",
    "categoryHeading1": "Gyratory compactor ",
    "categoryHeading2": "compactor ",
    "category": "<p>Gyratory compaction is used for precision compaction of asphalt samples to a specific target mixture or void content. Clients can get more precise readings of their samples to determine the mixture compatibility and mixture design properties.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/53696ec177ed429ca53e718f00a53b9e"
  },
  {
    "key": "e2601709-4379-4d78-9da8-dbe4b41539ab",
    "name": "Item 23",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "23",
    "categoryHeading1": "Model Mobile Load Simulator (MMLS 3)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Simulator (MMLS 3)",
    "category": "<p>An accelerated pavement testing tool applying realistic rolling wheel contact stress, to simulate traffic, moisture and temperature on the pavement layer that results in surface.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/2793abdc4ff9493e99f4e172d555567f"
  },
  {
    "key": "a7278d88-75e0-4836-af17-2e642ac6ee68",
    "name": "Item 24",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "24",
    "categoryHeading1": "Rolling straight edge",
    "categoryHeading2": "straight edge",
    "category": "<p>This method is used to determine the rideability of a specific road surface area and measure the transition between where processed sections join.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/b882faa0bb2c44dc914bb2b4b9224a71"
  },
  {
    "key": "de10d82d-d67b-4190-b051-4747452cd461",
    "name": "Item 25",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "25",
    "categoryHeading1": "Walking profilometer   ",
    "categoryHeading2": "profilometer   ",
    "category": "<p>Smaller scale application to measure surface roughness, texture and transition irregularities, and surface rutting.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/86a93ee1ae944aeb90e7ad8a9eca1856"
  },
  {
    "key": "90fd03aa-604f-4107-b818-6b6b9db52af3",
    "name": "Item 26",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "26",
    "categoryHeading1": "Falling Weight Deflectometer (FWD)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Deflectometer (FWD)",
    "category": "<p>The Falling Weight Deflectometer (FWD) is currently the most practical system for accurately measuring a pavement’s deflection response when it is subject to a dynamic load. It is also a non-destructive testing technique.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/aa82faa7bef64d5683670110af95461c"
  },
  {
    "key": "c66dc60b-9ff1-4080-9d9a-15417257890f",
    "name": "Item 27",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "27",
    "categoryHeading1": "International Roughness Index (IRI)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Roughness Index (IRI)",
    "category": "<p>Pave® Prof V2.0 is a modular system that uses 3D laser sensors to measure pavement profiles for applications such as highways and runways. It measures surface roughness, texture and rutting. It is capable of real-time continuous measurements of longitudinal and transverse profiles, rut depth and macro texture. These values can be used to calculate ride comfort, surface friction and surface noise generation to international standards.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/e8aa0b2821b2475ba2f2e3da43bda1e5"
  }
]]]></Value>
    </serviceCategories>
    <servicesButtons>
      <Value><![CDATA[[]]]></Value>
    </servicesButtons>
  </Properties>
</Content>